Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:05.30,Header,,0,0,0,,This is a Gentlemen of the Hàn free fansub.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.00,0:00:06.15,Episode Title,,0,0,0,,{\pos(635.966,327.272)\fade(255,0,255,0,900,3860,4780)}Episode 32
Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.00,0:00:06.15,Episode Title,,0,0,0,,{\pos(635.966,518.182)\fade(255,0,255,0,900,3860,4780)}Zhōu Yú Plans in Vain
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.54,0:00:12.38,Thinking,NTP,0,0,0,,Zhuge Liang, in order to cooperate with Wu to resist the Cao, crossed the river alone to Chaisang.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.74,0:00:16.02,Thinking,NTP,0,0,0,,He debated the assembled gentry and inspired Sun Quan,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.02,0:00:19.86,Thinking,NTP,0,0,0,,bolstering Marquis Sun's \Ndetermination to resist the Cao.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.02,0:00:23.98,Thinking,NTP,0,0,0,,But facing Cao Cao's massive army encroaching his borders,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.98,0:00:27.70,Thinking,NTP,0,0,0,,Sun Quan could not decide between war or peace.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.02,0:00:29.86,Thinking,NTP,0,0,0,,In his moment of indecision,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.86,0:00:34.86,Thinking,NTP,0,0,0,,he recalled the Commander of the Navy, \NZhou Yu, to discuss strategies together.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.77,0:00:34.98,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(360.336,458.182)\fade(255,0,255,0,400,3700,4100)}Sūn Quán \NStyled: Zhòngmóu
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.33,0:00:41.67,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(334.79,388.636)\fade(255,0,255,0,400,4700,5020)}Zhōu Yú \NStyled: Gōngjǐn
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.98,0:00:47.50,Default,,0,0,0,,My respects, Marquis of Wu!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.98,0:00:50.18,Default,,0,0,0,,No need, Gongjin.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.18,0:00:53.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Yesterday, Cao Mengde sent an envoy to deliver this letter.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.06,0:01:07.22,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord, have you discussed this with \Nthe military and civil officials?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.22,0:01:09.38,Default,,0,0,0,,We discussed it for days on end.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.74,0:01:16.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Some urged my surrender, others advocated for war.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.10,0:01:18.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, Gongjin, decide this matter on my behalf.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.94,0:01:22.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Who urged your surrender?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.58,0:01:27.42,Default,,0,0,0,,The civil officials all urged surrender.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.74,0:01:33.78,Default,,0,0,0,,I would hear your wise opinions, gentlemen.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.34,0:01:39.02,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Commander, Cao Mengde controls the Emperor\N in order to command the lords—
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.06,0:01:40.38,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(314.478,488.376)\fade(255,0,255,0,350,4660,5020)}Zhāng Zhāo \NStyled: Zǐbù
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.02,0:01:42.18,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,he acts in the Imperial Court's name.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.42,0:01:46.22,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,His might surges from taking over Jing Province.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.22,0:01:50.38,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,As of now, he has constructed \Nover a thousand heavy assault ships,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.22,0:01:50.38,Note (Potential style?),NTP,0,0,0,,AKA. Méngchōng (艨艟), "covered assaulter"
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.06,0:01:54.86,Default,,0,0,0,,As he advances by land and water, \Nhe will be difficult to stop.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.86,0:01:59.58,Default,,0,0,0,,It would be better to surrender for the moment, then plan thereafter.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.42,0:02:00.18,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(777.751,434.805)}Chéng Pǔ \NStyled: Démóu
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.62,0:02:04.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Who among us favors war?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.86,0:02:09.34,Default,,0,0,0,,All of us generals strongly propose war \Nin service to the Marquis of Wu.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.98,0:02:27.26,Default,,0,0,0,,This talk of surrender is but the discourse of pedants!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.46,0:02:32.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Our Eastern Wu has seen \Nthree generations since its founding!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.06,0:02:34.86,Default,,0,0,0,,How can we discard it like this?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.58,0:02:40.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Gongjin, what is the best plan to repel our foes?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.18,0:02:46.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}My liege, though Cao Cao is \Nformally the Chancellor of the Han,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.50,0:02:48.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}he is but its traitor!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.62,0:02:52.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}Our liege, with divine might and great talent, and with Sun Family's base,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.78,0:02:55.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}like a tiger of Jiangdong, with all its resources,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.14,0:02:58.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}should march across the realm, \Nexterminating the tyrannical!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.06,0:03:01.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}How could we surrender without a fight?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.50,0:03:10.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}Moreover, Cao Cao, by coming here in person, \Nhas broken the most important of military taboos.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.30,0:03:15.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}In the north, there are Ma Teng and Han Sui, \Nwho will be his future adversaries.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.22,0:03:19.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}Once we fight, both Ma and Han \Nwill attack him thereafter!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.10,0:03:21.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}This is traitor Cao's first taboo!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.54,0:03:24.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}The Cao army is unsuited for naval warfare.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.86,0:03:30.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}By leaving the saddles of horses to embark boats, \Ntheir combat ability will be greatly diminished.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.74,0:03:32.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}This is traitor Cao's second taboo!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.10,0:03:39.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}Presently, winter is setting in, \Nand the weather grows colder.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.86,0:03:44.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}The Cao army lacks adequate clothing and their horses lack fodder.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.86,0:03:47.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}This is traitor Cao's third taboo!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.54,0:03:50.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}The traitor has forced the northern men to travel far into the south.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.86,0:03:53.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}Being unfit for the southern lands, many will fall sick!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.54,0:03:55.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}This is traitor Cao's fourth taboo!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.30,0:04:02.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}Cao Cao violating these four taboos,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.02,0:04:07.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}he shall be defeated despite his many troops! \NMy lord, we will defeat Cao Cao today!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.38,0:04:17.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}I am willing to lead thousands of elite soldiers to invade Xiakou and defeat the Cao for you, my lord!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.02,0:04:26.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}That old traitor has long wanted to depose the Han Empire for himself,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.06,0:04:32.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}but he feared the Two Yuans, \NLiu Biao, Lü Bu, and me.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.58,0:04:37.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}Today, those heroes have perished, and only I remain!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.58,0:04:42.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}Sir, to attack the Cao\N aligns with my own intent.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.18,0:04:48.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909}It must be the Heaven's Will \Nto have you as my minister!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.18,0:04:55.74,Default,,0,0,0,,I would fight this bloody battle for my lord, \Nand risk my own life without hesitation!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.42,0:05:00.62,Default,,0,0,0,,I only fear that Your Lordship may still be hesitant.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.74,0:05:16.50,Default,,0,0,0,,I cannot share this world with that villain!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.50,0:05:20.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Any more who speak of surrender shall be dealt with like this table!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.97,0:05:24.98,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(292.93,504.935)}Huáng Gài \NStyled: Gōngfù
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.54,0:05:36.62,Default,,0,0,0,,I appoint Zhou Yu as {\i1}Chief Commander,{\i0} \Nwith command of the three armies by land and sea,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.78,0:05:39.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Cheng Pu as {\i1}Deputy Commander,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.54,0:05:42.78,Default,,0,0,0,,am Lu Su as {\i1}Adjutant Colonel!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.89,0:05:45.99,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,490.91)\fade(255,0,255,0,350,2450,2780)}Lǔ Sù \NStyled: Zǐjìng
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.90,0:05:49.50,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,From now on, any official, civil or military, \Nwho disobeys orders
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.50,0:05:51.18,Default,,0,0,0,,shall die by this sword!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.22,0:05:54.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, my liege!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.50,0:06:28.82,Default,,0,0,0,,By my lord's command, \NI shall lead our armies to defeat the Cao!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.82,0:06:31.82,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,You will receive your orders at the riverside camp by dawn!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.82,0:06:35.14,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,If you are late, you shall be punished according to military law!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.22,0:07:02.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Chief Commander, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.74,0:07:04.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir Kongming, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.02,0:07:12.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Please...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.38,0:07:26.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir Sleeping Dragon, after the discussion in court today, my lord is now resolute.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.38,0:07:32.14,Default,,0,0,0,,He has granted me the sword of command, \Nso I may strike down any who get in our way.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.86,0:07:37.94,Default,,0,0,0,,I would like to hear your \Nclever plan to defeat the Cao.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.65,0:07:44.59,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,5250,5620)\pos(953.045,506.494)}Zhūgé Liàng \NStyled: Kǒngmíng
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.14,0:07:42.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Chief Commander, forgive me for my frankness,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.06,0:07:46.78,Default,,0,0,0,,but in my opinion, General Sun still harbors doubts,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.14,0:07:48.94,Default,,0,0,0,,and he is not yet determined.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.74,0:08:01.58,Default,,0,0,0,,General Sun is worried about the power of the Cao army, and that we are outnumbered.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.02,0:08:07.38,Default,,0,0,0,,If you, sir, would compare the strengths and weaknesses of each side in a clear manner,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.70,0:08:13.18,Default,,0,0,0,,that would assuage his doubts, \Nand then we can succeed in the war.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.86,0:08:24.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Gongjin and Zijing, why visit so late in the night?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.34,0:08:29.86,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,My lord, regarding tomorrow's march,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.86,0:08:33.26,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,I wonder if you, sire, still feel doubt in your heart?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.22,0:08:36.86,Default,,0,0,0,,My will to fight is there,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.06,0:08:45.66,Default,,0,0,0,,but I am concerned about the power of \NCao Cao's army, and worry we are outnumbered.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.06,0:08:56.06,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord, be at ease, for I have already \Ndiscerned the true strength of the Cao force.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.78,0:09:01.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}They boast of having a million, \Nwhen they only have about 150,000 or 160,000;
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.66,0:09:03.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}they are also exhausted.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.66,0:09:06.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}Yuan Shao had 60,000 to 70,000 and Liu Biao had 20,000 to 30,000,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.78,0:09:08.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}but they were only 25,000 at their best.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.58,0:09:14.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}Their surrendered soldiers are disloyal, and their strength drained from prolonged warfare,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.86,0:09:17.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}so though the foe may be many, \Nthey are of no concern.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.66,0:09:21.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}My liege, you just need to give 50,000 troops to my command to crush Cao Cao!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.78,0:09:28.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}What you have said has caused my doubts to disappear!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.02,0:09:30.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}Now I am confident!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.34,0:09:39.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}Zibu and the others had no plan. \NThey have disappointed me.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.02,0:09:44.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}Only you, Zijing, and Cheng Pu share my plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.30,0:09:47.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}You all shall dispatch armies \Ntoward Sanjiangkou today!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.70,0:09:51.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}I shall continue to dispatch more troops to load more supplies and back you up!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.94,0:09:57.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}If your forces run into trouble, then I will lead a decisive battle against the traitor Cao myself!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.06,0:10:02.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.66,0:10:19.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Chief Commander.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.86,0:10:23.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Zijing.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.46,0:10:27.38,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord's clouds of worry have dispersed,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.38,0:10:32.66,Default,,0,0,0,,so why do you frown so?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.42,0:10:41.46,Default,,0,0,0,,That Zhuge Liang had already predicted my lord's own thoughts.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.86,0:10:50.18,Default,,0,0,0,,This man's ability in plotting and analysis exceed our own.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.70,0:10:54.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Left unchecked, he will become a danger to Eastern Wu in the future.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.86,0:10:58.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Unless... we eliminate him now!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.86,0:11:03.22,Default,,0,0,0,,We cannot! That villain Cao has yet to be defeated.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.62,0:11:07.26,Default,,0,0,0,,If we kill capable men now, \Nit will be like chopping our own arms off,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.26,0:11:10.30,Default,,0,0,0,,and we will lose trust with the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.66,0:11:17.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Yet if this man assists Liu Bei, \Nhe will eventually become our bitter enemy!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.86,0:11:22.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Zhuge Jin is his elder brother,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.14,0:11:28.22,Default,,0,0,0,,he could convince him to stay in Jiangdong \Nand join the Marquis of Wu. Would that not work?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.66,0:11:36.70,Default,,0,0,0,,If Zhuge Liang could serve Eastern Wu, \Nthat would be our lord's great fortune.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.26,0:11:42.34,Default,,0,0,0,,If we all work as one, then nothing can stop our great undertaking.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.30,0:11:45.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Only...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.86,0:12:06.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Chief Commander!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.22,0:12:29.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}The Chief Commander of Eastern Wu, Zhou Yu, \Nis leading troops to oppose the Cao!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.42,0:12:32.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}Now we shall have the Military Law recited to the entire army!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.98,0:12:37.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}The state law shows no intimacy; \Nthe military law shows no bonds!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.62,0:12:42.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}Those who violate them shall be dealt \Nwith the seven offenses and 54 gallows.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.10,0:12:47.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}The seven offenses are: Desultory, Disparity,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.30,0:12:51.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}Thievery, Deceit, Treachery,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.22,0:12:53.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}Disorder, and Neglect!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.38,0:12:55.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}Those dealt with the 54 gallows are:
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.66,0:12:58.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}those that act in cowardice,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.02,0:13:00.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}those that desert from the lines,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.46,0:13:02.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}those that disrespect orders,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.78,0:13:04.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}those that miss out on commands,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.10,0:13:07.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}those that delay food and pay,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.38,0:13:09.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}those that do not raise our flags,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.86,0:13:11.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}those that disobey the flag's wave,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.98,0:13:14.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}those that don't charge at the drums' beat,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.18,0:13:17.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}and those that don't retreat upon the bell's ring.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.58,0:13:33.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}Right now, the traitor Cao \Nabuses his liege and usurps power!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.18,0:13:36.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}He has imprisoned the Son of Heaven in Xuchang,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.86,0:13:39.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}and garrisons rowdy soldiers north of the Yangzi!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.38,0:13:45.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909}I have received orders to campaign, and hope you gentlemen fight hard when advancing!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.94,0:13:48.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}When our Great Army moves, \Ndo not disturb the people!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.82,0:13:52.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}The worthy will be awarded \Nand the violators punished without bias!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.62,0:13:58.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Where is Deputy Commander, Cheng Pu?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.93,0:14:09.43,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,360,2869,3180)\pos(351.093,441.836)}Chéng Zī
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.22,0:14:08.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Sire, my father, Cheng Pu, \Ncannot rise from bed due to a cold today,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.94,0:14:11.54,Default,,0,0,0,,so he has ordered me to serve in his stead.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.18,0:14:28.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Elder General Cheng suffers from illness in his \Nold age, yet still sends his son as a replacement.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.98,0:14:31.62,Default,,0,0,0,,He can be called a model for military discipline!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.30,0:14:42.02,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Return and tell your esteemed father
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.02,0:14:45.62,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,to wait until I am finished here, \Nthen I shall visit him right away.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.74,0:14:47.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.44,0:14:56.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Huang Gai and Han Dang, receive orders!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.34,0:14:58.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.18,0:15:10.50,Default,,0,0,0,,You two shall be the vanguard, to lead the warships and set camp at Sanjiangkou, effective immediately!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.98,0:15:11.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.22,0:15:17.82,Default,,0,0,0,,-Jiang Qin and Zhou Tai! \N-Here!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.82,0:15:19.86,Default,,0,0,0,,-You two shall be the second squad! \N-Yes sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.86,0:15:21.30,Default,,0,0,0,,-Ling Tong and Fan Zhang! \N-Here!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.30,0:15:23.06,Default,,0,0,0,,-You two shall be the third squad! \N-Yes sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.06,0:15:23.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Taishi Ci!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.14,0:15:24.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Here!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.86,0:15:25.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Lü Meng!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.90,0:15:26.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Here!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.54,0:15:27.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Lu Xun!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.74,0:15:28.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Here!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.38,0:15:29.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Dong Xi!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.30,0:15:29.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Here!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.78,0:15:32.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Lü Fan and Zhu Zhi!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.74,0:15:33.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Here!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.01,0:15:35.87,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(408.363,495.584)}Lǚ Fàn \NStyled: Zǐhéng
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.34,0:15:35.42,Default,,0,0,0,,-You shall be scout leaders! \N-Yes sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.86,0:15:42.86,Default,,0,0,0,,The armies of the six commanderies will advance on land and water, arriving by the deadline!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.18,0:15:46.38,Default,,0,0,0,,All remaining generals will be at standby, ready at any time!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.38,0:15:47.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.66,0:15:55.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Defeat the traitor Cao, \Nprotect our Jiangdong!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.70,0:16:08.18,Thinking,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Defeat the traitor Cao, \Nprotect our Jiangdong!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.34,0:16:19.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Father!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.86,0:16:22.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Son, how well does \NZhou the Youth appoint his generals?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.94,0:16:27.38,Default,,0,0,0,,He is strict with discipline and manages his men well. All the armies fully support him.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.62,0:16:34.86,Default,,0,0,0,,I always thought Zhou the Youth was but \Na feeble scholar, unfit for such a great task.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.10,0:16:38.86,Default,,0,0,0,,But he managed without issues! \NHe has a true talent for leadership!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.54,0:16:44.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, it looks like I have taken him too lightly.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.50,0:16:46.66,Default,,0,0,0,,He wants to personally visit you.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.06,0:16:49.06,Default,,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.38,0:16:52.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Hurry, follow me!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.86,0:17:01.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Chief Commander!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.18,0:17:03.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Cheng Pu has come before you to atone!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.94,0:17:08.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Cheng Pu has come before you to atone!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.38,0:17:11.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Elder General... Elder General Cheng, \Nwhy must you act so?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.38,0:17:12.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Please enter the camp!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.78,0:17:29.50,Default,,0,0,0,,I, Cheng Pu, am a veteran officer of Jiangdong, and yet the truth is,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.50,0:17:33.58,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,I have failed to live up to my lord \Nand the Chief Commander's expectations!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.94,0:17:35.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Not at all!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.86,0:17:43.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Your kindness, Elder General, has gained my respect!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.14,0:17:50.74,Default,,0,0,0,,I am young and unwise, and hope that you, the Elder General, teach and advise me still.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.74,0:17:53.06,Default,,0,0,0,,This has really shamed me!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.06,0:17:54.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Master Zhuge has arrived!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.14,0:17:59.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Since the Chief Commander is busy, \NI will take my leave for now.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.86,0:18:03.78,Default,,0,0,0,,I will come on time next morning \Nto await your assignment.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.82,0:18:09.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Elder General, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.14,0:18:14.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Chief Commander.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.86,0:18:16.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Master Zhuge!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.66,0:18:19.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Elder General, farewell!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.86,0:18:21.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Master Zhuge, please!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.18,0:18:29.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Meeting Gongjin is like drinking \Nfine wine; it is quite intoxicating!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.77,0:18:34.25,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(309.509,459.091)\fade(255,0,255,0,450,3000,3380)}Zhūgé Jǐn \NStyled: Zǐhéng
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.82,0:18:34.14,Default,,0,0,0,,For what task has \Nthe Chief Commander called upon me?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.14,0:18:36.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Master Zhuge, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.72,0:18:42.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Your younger brother, Kongming, \Nhas the ability to bolster kings.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.10,0:18:47.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Why has he lowered himself to serve Liu Bei?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.22,0:18:53.50,Default,,0,0,0,,It is fortunate that he is in Jiangdong, \NI would like to ask you to persuade him
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.34,0:18:57.10,Default,,0,0,0,,to abandon Liu Bei and work for Eastern Wu instead!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.86,0:19:04.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Thus, our liege will gain a talented official, \Nand you two brothers can see each other again!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.38,0:19:07.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Would that not be perfect?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.82,0:19:11.50,Default,,0,0,0,,I receive great favor from the Marquis of Wu \Nand think of repaying him every day.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.50,0:19:14.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Now that you have orders for me, \Nhow could I not make every effort?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.02,0:19:28.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Second Brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.46,0:19:32.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Elder Brother, due to the state affairs of our nations, it has been difficult to visit.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.66,0:19:37.22,Default,,0,0,0,,But now you have deigned to visit me, I am regretful!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.22,0:19:39.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Second Brother, please rise quickly...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.34,0:19:42.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Elder Brother, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.50,0:19:49.42,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Since I have left home to be here, there is \Nno moment I did not miss you, my younger brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.58,0:19:52.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:52.34,0:19:53.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.50,0:20:05.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Elder Brother, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.22,0:20:14.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}Second Brother, have you heard of {\i1}Bóyí and Shūqí?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.22,0:20:21.82,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Note: Bóyí(伯夷) and Shūqí(叔齐) were royal sons of Guzhu, a vassal state of the Shang Dynasty, known for their moral virtue and loyalty to each other and their state, even as it fell to Zhōu.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.22,0:20:21.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}Those two are virtuous men of old!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.10,0:20:26.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}Boyi and Shuqi never separated in their lifetime.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.46,0:20:31.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}Although they later starved to death at \NMount Shouyang, the brothers were still together.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.02,0:20:34.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}We came from the same womb,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.54,0:20:38.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}yet we serve different lords, \Nso we are unable to get together at any time.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.50,0:20:43.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}Remembering those ancients, how can I not be ashamed?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.98,0:20:51.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}Your words are about love; my service is about duty.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.58,0:20:56.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}Boyi and Shuqi were Shang ministers and refused the grains of Zhōu.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.58,0:20:56.42,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Note: referring to chengyu idiom "不食周粟 "
Dialogue: 0,0:20:56.66,0:21:01.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}We brothers are Hàn Empire's ministers, and Imperial Uncle Liu is a scion of the dynasty.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.86,0:21:08.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}Elder Brother, if you can leave Eastern Wu and join me in serving Imperial Uncle Liu,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.18,0:21:11.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}above, you can be a proud consul of Han; below, familial blood can meet again.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.62,0:21:14.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}Would this not fulfill both love and duty?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.90,0:21:18.98,Default,,0,0,0,,You!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.98,0:21:26.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Master Zhuge?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.54,0:21:31.38,Default,,0,0,0,,What did Kongming think?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.26,0:21:37.06,Default,,0,0,0,,I went to convince him, but he silenced me instead.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.54,0:21:42.94,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord offers me great grace, so how could I abandon him?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:44.02,0:21:47.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, you have been faithful to our liege, \Nthere is no need to say more!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:47.82,0:21:52.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I... have my own method to \Ngain Kongming's submission...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:18.42,0:22:19.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Commander!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:20.26,0:22:20.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Commander!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:20.82,0:22:24.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Pass my orders! Each squad shall set camp at their positions.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:24.54,0:22:27.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Have the vanguards meet me at camp for a conference.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:27.30,0:22:28.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:32.66,0:22:33.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Mister Wolong.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:35.42,0:22:36.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Chief Commander.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:38.06,0:22:40.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}When the Yuan and Cao fought in the past,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:41.02,0:22:43.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}Cao Cao was able to triumph despite having few troops.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:43.90,0:22:49.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}This is all due to his use of Xu You's plan, \Nby first destroying supplies at Wuchao.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:51.18,0:22:56.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}Now the Cao army numbers 830,000, and my army is just 50,000 or 60,000. How can I resist him?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:57.34,0:23:00.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}I think to emulate Xu You's plan,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:00.46,0:23:05.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}by first destroying their supplies, thereby \Ndisturbing their morale. Then we would succeed.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:07.02,0:23:11.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}I have ascertained that the Cao army stored their grain at Mount Jutie.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:11.90,0:23:15.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}Sir has lived in the Central Plains, \Nso you are familiar with the land.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:15.66,0:23:19.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}I'd like to ask you to lead Generals Guan, Zhang, and Zilong,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:19.18,0:23:22.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}and I will also provide 1,000 troops for your use.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:22.06,0:23:25.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}Go to Mount Jutie overnight \Nand destroy the traitor Cao's supplies.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:26.22,0:23:29.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}This is a mutual benefit for both the Sun and Liu families.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:30.22,0:23:32.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}Sir, I hope you will not decline.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:34.50,0:23:39.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, it is not too late for it. \NI hope you can quickly send the 1,000 troops.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.06,0:23:41.58,Default,,0,0,0,,I will leave tomorrow!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:54.86,0:23:58.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Chief Commander, you have sent \NZhuge Liang to cut off supplies.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:58.78,0:24:00.38,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you intend?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:02.70,0:24:06.34,Default,,0,0,0,,If I were to kill Kongming, I would be the ridicule of the people,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:06.82,0:24:11.46,Default,,0,0,0,,so if I use Cao Cao's hands to kill him, \Nthat would remove a future threat.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:26.70,0:24:29.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, you seem to be in good spirits!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:32.58,0:24:36.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Zijing, have you come to see me off?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:38.22,0:24:41.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, if you leave, \Nis it possible for you to succeed or not?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:41.66,0:24:44.86,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,In tactics of water, land, chariots, and cavalry,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:44.86,0:24:48.42,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,I am learned in all of them. \NWhy worry about failure?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:50.22,0:24:55.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Perhaps those like you, sir, \Nand Zhou the Youth are only skilled in one?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:59.46,0:25:03.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Me and Gongjin... \Nhow are we only skilled in one?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:03.82,0:25:07.02,Default,,0,0,0,,I have long heard of a children's song which sang like:
Dialogue: 0,0:25:07.02,0:25:10.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}"For ambushes and gate guarding there's Zijing;"
Dialogue: 0,0:25:10.78,0:25:14.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}"For naval combat there's Zhou the Youth."
Dialogue: 0,0:25:15.46,0:25:18.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}Sir, your land troops are only able to guard passes
Dialogue: 0,0:25:18.74,0:25:20.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}and set up ambushes, that is all.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:21.02,0:25:24.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}As for Zhou Gongjin, he is only good at naval warfare,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:24.46,0:25:26.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}unfit for land battles, that is all!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:32.34,0:25:36.10,Default,,0,0,0,,That Zhuge Liang dares say \NI'm incapable at land battles?!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:37.62,0:25:42.06,Default,,0,0,0,,I do not need him to go! \NI shall lead 10,000 soldiers towards Mount Jutie,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:42.06,0:25:43.66,Default,,0,0,0,,and cut off the bastard's route!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:44.22,0:25:46.26,Default,,0,0,0,,See whether I succeed or not!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:52.66,0:25:53.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:55.22,0:25:55.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Zijing.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:55.82,0:25:56.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:59.34,0:26:04.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Gongjin ordered me to cut off supplies, but \Nactually wanted to use that traitor's blade to kill me.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:05.42,0:26:10.14,Default,,0,0,0,,I only used a few words to humor him, \Nbut Gongjin couldn't tolerate that.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:10.14,0:26:11.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir...
Dialogue: 0,0:26:11.66,0:26:13.70,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the time to utilize people.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:13.70,0:26:18.46,Default,,0,0,0,,I hope the Marquis of Wu and Lord Liu will \Njoin forces and mind to fulfill this great feat,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:20.66,0:26:25.34,Default,,0,0,0,,but if we have this sort of infighting, \Nwhat will become of our cause?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:27.62,0:26:29.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, your words are mistaken!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:29.50,0:26:34.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Cao Cao is intelligent and crafty. He is used to cutting off people's supply routes.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:34.18,0:26:36.78,Default,,0,0,0,,How can he not be guarded by heavy troops now?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:37.58,0:26:40.70,Default,,0,0,0,,If Gongjin goes, he will surely be captured.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:42.02,0:26:45.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Right now, he should first \Nengage in naval warfare and win.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:45.34,0:26:50.34,Default,,0,0,0,,That would frustrate the morale of the northern army; he will find other strategies to crush them.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:50.94,0:26:54.22,Default,,0,0,0,,I hope you will use kind words to advise Gongjin.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:55.02,0:26:56.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Certainly, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:12.02,0:27:15.42,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,That man's cunning far outclasses my own.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:16.14,0:27:19.62,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Eventually, he will be a menace for Eastern Wu!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:21.66,0:27:28.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Chief Commander, this is the time to utilize people. \NI hope you will prioritize our nation.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:29.02,0:27:32.26,Default,,0,0,0,,After we defeat Cao Cao, \Nit would not be too late to plot again.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:36.22,0:27:37.74,Default,,0,0,0,,I yield to you then.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:39.86,0:27:43.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, Liu Bei sent Mi Zhu to ferry support to the army!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:48.86,0:27:49.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Let him in!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:50.86,0:27:52.22,Default,,0,0,0,,We invite Mister Mi!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:05.14,0:28:07.30,Default,,0,0,0,,My respects, Chief Commander.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:07.30,0:28:12.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I was ordered by Lord Liu to present \Ncattle, sheep, and fine wine. May you accept it!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:10.58,0:28:12.83,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(948.429,495.584)}Mí Zhú \NStyled: Zǐzhòng
Dialogue: 0,0:28:13.38,0:28:14.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Please?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:14.26,0:28:14.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:23.86,0:28:26.98,Default,,0,0,0,,How fares Lord Xuande recently?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:26.98,0:28:32.22,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,My lord was most pleased when he heard you set camp at Sanjiangkou!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:33.06,0:28:38.86,Default,,0,0,0,,However, Mister Kongming has left Jiangxia \Nfor a long while, and my lord misses him greatly.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:39.22,0:28:42.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Please allow him to join me on my journey back.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:45.82,0:28:51.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Kongming and I were just discussing ways \Nto defeat Cao Cao. How can that be left unfinished?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:53.14,0:28:57.66,Default,,0,0,0,,I am most grateful for Lord Xuande's kindness.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:57.66,0:29:03.06,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,I should have ferried across to thank him myself, \Nbut with military duties, I am unable to.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:04.86,0:29:11.46,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,If Lord Xuande could ferry across and meet with me, I would hear what he has to say.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:12.82,0:29:16.90,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Allow me to return and convey your wish to my lord.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:16.90,0:29:19.46,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,I, Mi Zhu, take my leave.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:24.86,0:29:27.66,Default,,0,0,0,,-No need to see me off! \N-Mister Mi, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:32.66,0:29:37.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Chief Commander, what do you intend \Nto do when you meet with Liu Xuande?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:40.34,0:29:45.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Liu Bei is a mighty raptor of our time. \NHe has to be eliminated!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:46.14,0:29:51.22,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,I plan to kill him when he's crossed the river, thus removing a future threat to Eastern Wu!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:51.22,0:29:52.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Chief Commander!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:53.06,0:29:54.86,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,A decisive battle is imminent!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:54.86,0:29:58.38,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Liu Bei is garrisoned at Jiangxia and we can trap Cao Cao then!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:58.94,0:30:05.26,Default,,0,0,0,,But if you proceed with your plan, \Nwould that not be to our enemies' benefit?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:05.26,0:30:09.30,Default,,0,0,0,,If Liu Bei ferries across, \NI will first welcome him with a feast,
Dialogue: 0,0:30:09.30,0:30:12.54,Default,,0,0,0,,and entertain him with music and dances.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:15.78,0:30:18.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Zijing, depart.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:20.42,0:30:21.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:44.54,0:30:51.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Elder Brother, Zhou Yu is a man of cunning tricks, \Nwe have also not received letters from the Strategos.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:47.66,0:30:54.82,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,6500,6860)\pos(326.326,491.81)}Guān Yǔ \NStyled: Yúncháng
Dialogue: 0,0:30:52.14,0:30:54.26,Default,,0,0,0,,I fear that it is a trap.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:54.98,0:30:56.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Should you really be going?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:57.06,0:31:02.02,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(306.782,503.377)\fade(255,0,255,0,350,4300,4620)}Liú Bèi \NStyled: Xuándé
Dialogue: 0,0:30:57.14,0:31:02.26,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,I need to cooperate with Wu against the Cao, and Zhou the Youth requested my presence.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:02.26,0:31:06.26,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Should I not go, that would break trust in our alliance.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:06.90,0:31:10.18,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,If both sides doubt each other, \Nthat would ruin our great cause.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:11.14,0:31:14.78,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,I will have Second Brother follow me, \Nthen there will be no issues.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:14.78,0:31:17.74,Default,,0,0,0,,If so, wouldn't it be best for us to come with?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:15.18,0:31:18.18,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,2460,2800)\pos(773.338,531.429)}Zhāng Fēi \NStyled: Yìdé
Dialogue: 0,0:31:20.14,0:31:23.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Third Brother and Zilong, \Nyou both need to defend the cities.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:23.74,0:31:25.58,Default,,0,0,0,,I shall return shortly.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:25.82,0:31:31.22,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(812.101,501.819)\fade(255,0,255,0,350,4750,5100)}Zhào Yún \NStyled: Zǐlóng
Dialogue: 0,0:31:25.58,0:31:27.94,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Zilong always handles affairs with care.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:27.94,0:31:30.90,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Urge Yide not to be imprudent.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:31.54,0:31:32.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:35.66,0:31:38.10,Default,,0,0,0,,How many men accompany Liu Bei?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:38.50,0:31:40.06,Default,,0,0,0,,He has just over twenty men!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:44.46,0:31:45.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Heed me!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:45.78,0:31:49.78,Default,,0,0,0,,During the feast, take me throwing the cup \Nas the signal! Do not fail this!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:49.78,0:31:50.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:04.78,0:32:08.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Zhou Gongjin is a true commander!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:10.82,0:32:13.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Elder Brother, Commander Zhou has left his camp to welcome us.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:37.22,0:32:40.34,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Lord Xuande, you deigned to ferry across. I feel most honored!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:40.34,0:32:43.06,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,I hope you will forgive me for not coming earlier.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:44.34,0:32:47.14,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Your order and discipline is well known!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:47.14,0:32:50.70,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,In comparison I am but feeble, \Nwhy treat me with great courtesy?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:56.50,0:33:00.06,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Lord Xuande, you are a hero of this age. \NMy respects befit such a figure.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:00.06,0:33:01.82,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Men! Prepare the feast!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:01.82,0:33:02.58,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:03.34,0:33:04.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Please?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:04.78,0:33:05.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:26.30,0:33:28.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Mister Wolong!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:28.74,0:33:30.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Mister Wolong!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:31.42,0:33:32.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Zijing?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:33.26,0:33:34.78,Default,,0,0,0,,What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:39.78,0:33:40.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:42.50,0:33:43.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Is that so?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:44.30,0:33:45.46,Default,,0,0,0,,That...
Dialogue: 0,0:33:50.34,0:33:54.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Why does that music carry \Nsuch a malevolent feeling to it?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:54.42,0:33:55.46,Default,,0,0,0,,That...
Dialogue: 0,0:33:58.94,0:34:00.74,Default,,0,0,0,,That is {\i1}the Bāyú Dance!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:58.94,0:34:06.22,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Note: Bāyú Dance is a music and dance form using weapons and shields, practiced by the Bǎndùn-Mán peoples of modern-day Sichuan.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:01.90,0:34:04.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Zijing, who is being entertained in that tent?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:09.54,0:34:12.10,Default,,0,0,0,,It's Lord Liu.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:14.46,0:34:15.94,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord is in danger!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:16.30,0:34:19.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Zijing, why didn't you tell me earlier!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:19.42,0:34:21.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Mister Kongming! Mister Kongming!
Dialogue: 0,0:35:29.78,0:35:30.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Lord Xuande?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:32.82,0:35:33.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Please?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:33.62,0:35:34.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:00.74,0:36:01.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Let us go.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:03.10,0:36:06.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}My lord is not in danger anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:19.14,0:36:20.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Please?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:43.94,0:36:47.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Chief Commander, why still your cup so?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:48.82,0:36:49.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Let us drink!
Dialogue: 0,0:37:10.86,0:37:14.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Lord Xuande, who is that man standing beside you?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:17.06,0:37:19.46,Default,,0,0,0,,That is my younger brother, Guan Yunchang!
Dialogue: 0,0:37:20.86,0:37:24.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Is that not the Guan Yunchang \Nwho slew Yan Liang and Wen Chou?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:25.78,0:37:26.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Indeed!
Dialogue: 0,0:37:34.22,0:37:36.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Apologies, apologies!
Dialogue: 0,0:37:58.78,0:38:00.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Chief Commander,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:02.14,0:38:06.98,Default,,0,0,0,,me and Kongming have not seen each other for several days. May you invite him to come?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:08.58,0:38:11.06,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Kongming is not here right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:11.38,0:38:15.70,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,After we defeat Cao Cao, it would not be too late to meet with Kongming.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:17.06,0:38:18.10,Default,,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:38:18.62,0:38:20.86,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Then I must bid farewell for now.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:20.86,0:38:24.14,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,After I defeat our foe, I will return to celebrate.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:25.78,0:38:27.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I am busy with military affairs.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:28.14,0:38:32.62,Default,,0,0,0,,It would be inconvenient for you to stay, so forgive me for that.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:32.94,0:38:33.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Goodbye.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:00.30,0:39:01.18,Default,,0,0,0,,My liege!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:04.50,0:39:05.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Please sit!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:07.06,0:39:08.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Strategos, please sit!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:10.58,0:39:15.06,Default,,0,0,0,,My liege, are you aware that you were in danger today?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:16.14,0:39:17.58,Default,,0,0,0,,What danger was there?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:18.14,0:39:23.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Were it not for Yunchang's presence, \Nyou would have been killed by Zhou the Youth.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:28.30,0:39:32.10,Default,,0,0,0,,If it is this dangerous, then you must hurry back to Jiangxia!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:34.14,0:39:37.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}I may be in a tiger's maw, \Nbut I am unshakable as Mount Tai.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:37.74,0:39:43.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}After you return, mobilize warships and cavalry immediately to prepare for Cao Cao's defeat.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:43.34,0:39:46.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}When it is the {\i1}jiazi{\i0} day of the 12th month,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:46.06,0:39:50.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.879}order Zilong to ride a small boat and wait on the south banks.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:50.42,0:39:52.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord10.909\pos(640,666.666)}There must be no mistake!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:53.46,0:39:55.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Strategos, what do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:40:01.86,0:40:05.30,Default,,0,0,0,,My liege, please leave at once. I fear possible dangers this evening.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:20.22,0:40:21.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Strategos, take care!
Dialogue: 0,0:40:24.06,0:40:27.82,Default,,0,0,0,,My liege, do not forget my advice!

